          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नाव (nāv) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from nāvā, \"boat\". CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry (CDIAL 7081); the match is through Gujarati nāv. English navy goes back, through Latin navis, to the same ancient word."
            }
